WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.720
Pause token KV compression shrinks cache 3.5 times and speeds H100 inference 3.2 times on long math problems. This is Models &amp; Agents Episode 205. A bridge KV trains a model to compress each completed block of generated chain of thought into the key value cache entries of a few learned pause tokens that produce no output, according to a paper on archive. Those pause tokens receive positions inside the replace block. Cash budget is allocated by measured layer value.

00:00:29.720 --> 00:00:38.060
and compression runs on relatively large blocks. On 446 problems from AM, AMT, AMC and similar

00:00:38.060 --> 00:00:44.120
contests with 32,000 token generations, keeping one quarter of the cash matches and identically

00:00:44.120 --> 00:00:47.880
trained full key value model in both accuracy and output length.

00:00:48.540 --> 00:00:53.220
The strongest published eviction baseline at the same budget produces far longer outputs.

00:00:53.220 --> 00:00:57.280
A retrained compressor baseline loses 10 accuracy points.

00:00:57.740 --> 00:01:03.560
Served in VLLM, that pause token compressor runs per sequence on a saturated H100.

00:01:04.548 --> 00:01:10.148
CoteS uses probability competition between the two most likely tokens to allocate continuous weight

00:01:10.148 --> 00:01:13.448
between discrete commitment and soft exploration at each step,

00:01:13.948 --> 00:01:15.468
and it needs no extra training.

00:01:16.088 --> 00:01:19.788
An archive paper says the second candidate represents the strongest alternative,

00:01:19.788 --> 00:01:24.528
so larger separation signals stability and keeps the representation close

00:01:24.528 --> 00:01:25.628
to the sampled token.

00:01:26.248 --> 00:01:30.128
Smaller separation increases the soft contribution to retain alternatives.

00:01:30.688 --> 00:01:34.568
The method requires no extra forward passes or tuned thresholds.

00:01:34.828 --> 00:01:39.408
Experiments across six reasoning benchmarks show consistent gains over standard chain of

00:01:39.408 --> 00:01:42.208
thought and prior training-free latent methods.

00:01:43.119 --> 00:01:48.719
Woolhoff, a language spoken by 23 million people, mainly in Senegal, now has open-weight

00:01:48.719 --> 00:01:52.179
models from 0.6 billion to 14 billion parameters.

00:01:52.639 --> 00:01:57.099
The archive release instruction tunes, preference aligns, and merges those weights.

00:01:57.579 --> 00:02:01.979
And after the full pipeline, the 8 billion and 14 billion variants remain competitive

00:02:01.979 --> 00:02:07.319
with much larger commercial systems on 63 public and internal tasks while preserving

00:02:07.319 --> 00:02:08.619
cross-lingual performance.

00:02:09.259 --> 00:02:13.579
The models are already an internal customer care pilots and available on hugging face.

